<%#
  Shown when an admin adds a payment to an order from the backend.

  There is deliberately no card-number form here. A new card must be entered in
  the customer's own browser (Square's Web Payments SDK); an admin typing a card
  number into this page would mean card data hitting our server, which CLAUDE.md
  forbids outright.

  What an admin CAN do is charge a card the customer saved with Square. Those
  are listed below (SquareCreditCard#reusable_sources). Solidus's admin
  payments controller reads the chosen card from params[:card] -- the same
  param its stock card form uses -- and the charge goes to Square's card on file.
  The customer agreed to phone/admin charges when they saved the card (see
  nsb.checkout.save_card_consent).
%>
<% saved_cards = previous_cards %>

<div class="square-admin-source">
  <% if saved_cards.any? %>
    <fieldset class="no-border-bottom">
      <legend>Charge a saved card</legend>
      <div class="field" data-hook="previous_cards">
        <% saved_cards.each do |card| %>
          <label>
            <%= radio_button_tag :card, card.id, card == saved_cards.first %>
            <%= card.cc_type.presence&.titleize || "Card" %> ending <%= card.last_digits %>
            <% if card.month.present? && card.year.present? %>
              (expires <%= format("%02d", card.month.to_i) %>/<%= card.year %>)
            <% end %>
          </label><br>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <p><small>The amount above is charged to the selected card through Square.</small></p>
    </fieldset>
  <% else %>
    <p><strong>This customer has no saved card.</strong></p>
  <% end %>

  <p>
    A new card cannot be keyed in here: Square requires it to be entered in the
    customer's own browser. To use a new card, either:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>ask the customer to complete checkout in the portal (they can tick
      "Save this card" so you can charge it from here next time), or</li>
    <li>take the payment in the Square dashboard or Square app, then record it
      against this order using the <em>Check</em> payment method with the Square
      receipt number in the notes.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <small>Refunds for card payments taken through the portal can be issued from
    the Payments tab, and will be sent to Square.</small>
  </p>
</div>
